{:event/id "e35914ef-c820-451c-9db9-eebfba862695" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:7eb79274-9336-4767-8660-7d5c674fe0eb" :event/seq 1 :event/causes ["7eb79274-9336-4767-8660-7d5c674fe0eb"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:7eb79274-9336-4767-8660-7d5c674fe0eb" :event/at "2026-09-14T14:10:03Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/mcp-ingress-is-guarded-grant-admission :finding/shapes #{:gate :capability :protocol :policy} :finding/current-name "trusted-loopback-grant + grant-of" :finding/candidate-name "GuardedGrantAdmission<Request,Grant>" :finding/claim "Authentication methods do not make transport data authoritative merely because a token string is present. The selected method must be enabled for the surface, every declared environment/transport/secret guard must pass, and the method must yield a nonblank identity plus tool grant; missing contracts, guards, or grants refuse admission. The reusable law is that ingress proof and resulting capability grant are separate values joined only by an explicit fail-closed admission decision."}}
{:event/id "5f989c72-8e73-4982-83a6-c8d7c1b28592" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:7eb79274-9336-4767-8660-7d5c674fe0eb" :event/seq 2 :event/causes ["e35914ef-c820-451c-9db9-eebfba862695"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:7eb79274-9336-4767-8660-7d5c674fe0eb" :event/at "2026-09-14T14:10:03Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/mcp-token-actor-is-revalidated-binding :finding/shapes #{:credential :identity :revocation :resolver} :finding/current-name "token-actor-honourable? + call-actor-id" :finding/candidate-name "RevalidatedActorBinding<Token,Membership>" :finding/claim "An MCP bearer token may carry an actor, but each request resolves the token owner through current policy state and compares the claimed actor with the membership stored actor binding. Reassignment is a refusal rather than a silent switch, and an older token carrying no actor remains actorless instead of inheriting a newer membership actor. The durable credential is therefore evidence to revalidate, not a timeless authority snapshot."}}
{:event/id "e167c170-c86a-4de7-9b99-bfe2c0a675b1" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:7eb79274-9336-4767-8660-7d5c674fe0eb" :event/seq 3 :event/causes ["5f989c72-8e73-4982-83a6-c8d7c1b28592"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:7eb79274-9336-4767-8660-7d5c674fe0eb" :event/at "2026-09-14T14:10:03Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/mcp-post-remints-request-scoped-authority :finding/shapes #{:capability :lifecycle :adapter :boundary} :finding/current-name "serve-mcp-post! + resolve-token-context!" :finding/candidate-name "RequestScopedAuthorityRemint<Credential,Context>" :finding/claim "After credential admission, an MCP POST resolves a fresh policy context from the token record, derives the acting identity from current binding, and constructs a new in-process MCP server and tool surface for that request. The serialized token crosses the process boundary, but executable authority is materialized only after local revalidation. This pressure-tests ProcessLocalAuthoritySeal as a stronger implementation of the broader law that durable credential evidence and executable process authority are not the same object."}}
